# Copy to .env and pass it explicitly (the app doesn't read .env by itself):
#   uv run --env-file .env agent-orchestrator    |    docker run --env-file .env ...
# Without any of these, agents.yaml runs on a local Ollama (qwen3.5:9b).

# --- Free hosted demo: Groq first, OpenRouter :free as backup -----------------------
# A list (comma separated) is an ordered fallback chain: 429 / 5xx / timeout on the
# first provider moves on to the next one. One name = that provider only.
COORDINATOR_PROVIDER=groq,openrouter
WORKER_PROVIDER=groq,openrouter

GROQ_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Groq, free plan. Tool use: https://console.groq.com/docs/tool-use
# Limits (per model, so coordinator and workers on different models don't share a
# quota): https://console.groq.com/docs/rate-limits -> gpt-oss-120b / gpt-oss-20b /
# qwen3.8-27b: 30 RPM, 1K RPD, 8K TPM. llama-3.3-70b-versatile and llama-3.1-8b-instant
# now show "Contact sales" on https://console.groq.com/docs/models.
# gpt-oss models (production) don't do parallel tool calls on Groq, so the coordinator
# delegates one worker at a time. qwen/qwen3.8-27b does parallel calls but is a preview
# model (can be removed at short notice).
GROQ_COORDINATOR_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
GROQ_WORKER_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b

# OpenRouter :free models whose supported_parameters include tools and tool_choice, from
# https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models (checked 2026-11-09). Free limits
# (https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/reference/limits): 20 RPM, and only 50 requests/day
# unless the account ever bought >= 10 credits (then 1,000/day).
# Alternative coordinator: nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free
OPENROUTER_COORDINATOR_MODEL=google/gemma-4-31b-it:free
OPENROUTER_WORKER_MODEL=google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it:free

# --- Other providers ----------------------------------------------------------------
# COORDINATOR_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# COORDINATOR_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
